 "brief": "# Amber chat: one UI asset + rename Gizmo -> Amber (Brett, Nov 7)\n\nRule: every UI element is an asset. The AmberX companion chat (apps/amberx-droid/src/plugins/companion/web: Chat.tsx, index.tsx, companion.css) is a plain component. Styling already uses tokens (no hard-coded values) — keep it that way.\n\n## 1. Chat as an asset (Fable: contract)\n- Define/extend the shared chat UI asset type (reuse an existing chat/build-chat@1/assistant asset type if one fits; else a new `chat-view@1` in framework/assets with schema, both validators, fixture, check). Covers layout, message bubbles, input bar, voice/talk controls, header, empty/no-provider states.\n- Chat.tsx renders from the asset. The console AI assistant chat should be able to use the same asset (same assistant@1 plugin backs both).\n\n## 2. Rename Gizmo -> Amber, safely\n- Inventory every `gizmo` reference first (code, ids, settings keys, storage paths, docs, persona, voice). Save the list in the report.\n- Rename to Amber everywhere: ids, files, labels, persona, voice.\n- Migrate saved chats/settings to new keys; dry-run the migration on a copy first and verify it loads.\n- Keep `gizmo` as an alias that resolves to Amber (old links/settings/commands keep working).\n- Back up old data; one-step rollback.\n- CI check: fails if `gizmo` appears anywhere except the alias table and migration.\n\n## 3. UI Review with choices\n- Submit THREE distinct looks for the Amber chat (phone + desktop shots) to UI Review with --choices, so Brett picks one in the Choices tab. The pick becomes the asset's default.\n\n## 4. Tests + Shipped features\nAll AmberX + console tests green; add to Shipped features.\n\nProgress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push. No hard-coded styling.\n## Addendum (Brett, Nov 7): a full Claude.ai replacement\nRight now the chat is crap. Bar: as good as claude.ai, phone and desktop.\n- Desktop: a left navigation sidebar (new chat, chat history with search, pinned, projects/blueprints, agents, settings), collapsible; phone: slide-out drawer.\n- Polished: markdown, code blocks with copy, images/files, streaming, stop/regenerate/edit, model + agent picker, voice/talk button, long-chat performance.\n- All from assets (nav, sidebar, bubbles, input bar each their own asset), no hard-coded styling.\n- UI Review: three full-screen looks, desktop + phone (--choices).\n\n## Addendum 2 (Brett, Nov 7): go crazy, entirely new design\n- Turn the chat's style override ON and give it an entirely NEW design: new colour theme + new style theme (its own theme/skin assets), not the app's. Changes only the chat (override rule).\n- 10 distinct layouts (e.g. sidebar classic, floating dock, split canvas, minimal focus, cards, terminal-style, command-palette-first, threaded, bubble-heavy mobile, dashboard) and many options per piece (bubbles, input bar, header, sidebar, buttons, voice controls).\n- Send them all to UI Review as choice sets (--choices) so Brett picks layout, theme, style and each piece. Desktop + phone shots each.\n",
